.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt MAILX 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mailx
.Nd local mbox and Maildir mail reader and sender
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar mailbox
.Op Fl s Ar subject
.Op Fl b Ar body-file
.Ar recipient ...
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar mailbox
.Op Fl H | e | r Ar N | d Ar N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the POSIX
.Nm
front end over the bounded local mail core.
It supports local mbox and Maildir delivery, header listing, reading, deletion and the
existence check; it does not implement SMTP, a network MTA, reply, forward, cc/bcc, attachments
or an interactive prompt.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s Ar subject
Subject for an outgoing message.
.It Fl b Ar body-file
Read the body from
.Ar body-file ;
.Li -
means standard input.
.It Fl f Ar mailbox
Select the mbox file or Maildir.
.It Fl H
List headers.
.It Fl e
Exit 0 when at least one message exists.
.It Fl r Ar N
Read message
.Ar N .
.It Fl d Ar N
Delete message
.Ar N .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MAIL
.It Ev MAIL
Default mailbox when
.Fl f
is absent.
.It Ev USER , LOGNAME
Sender name used in the local
.Li From:
header.
.It Ev HOME
Base for the default Maildir/mbox selection.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width $HOME/Maildir
.It Pa $HOME/Maildir
Preferred default Maildir.
.It Pa $HOME/mbox
Fallback mbox.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error or an unsupported option exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mail 1
.Sh BUGS
Reply, forward, SMTP/network delivery, cc/bcc, attachments and an interactive prompt are not
implemented.
